"body": "Once scrolled, the room kept for the sign-in button pushed the search box onto a second row at 1280 wide.\n\nOn screens wider than 900px the slim header's links now sit a little closer. Local build, measured in a real browser: 1280 wide goes from 2 rows (96px) to 1 row (56px); 1440 and 1920 stay at 1 row; 0 overlaps with the sign-in button at 5 widths. 1024 and 1100 still take 2 rows.",
